  "headline": {
    "1_hybrid_is_decisive": "recall@10 0.825 -> 0.950, MRR 0.618 -> 0.785, nDCG 0.668 -> 0.826, pack_recall 0.950 -> 1.000. Embeddings earn their cost on this corpus; this is the column missing from the raw-vs-lexical comparison.",
    "2_device_matters_for_indexing_not_querying": "Indexing this corpus: CPU ~55 min vs GPU 22.9 s (145x). Query p50: 205.7 ms vs 167.4 ms (1.2x). A single short query cannot fill a GPU; bulk indexing can. Index on GPU, query on either.",
    "3_vec0_is_not_a_speedup_here": "Identical accuracy to exact (0.950/0.785/0.826 both) and 156 ms vs 167 ms p50 -- noise at 1713 chunks. Consistent with the 100k synthetic benchmark: vec0 is a constant-factor C-loop win, not ANN.",
    "4_rerank_makes_retrieval_worse": "recall@10 0.950 -> 0.875, MRR 0.785 -> 0.555, nDCG 0.826 -> 0.632, AND p50 167 ms -> 16,772 ms (100x). A double negative. bge-reranker-v2-m3 is a general MS-Marco cross-encoder, not code-tuned, so re-scoring a good fused ranking discards signal.",
    "5_rerank_latency_two_known_causes": "CrossEncoder loads at max_seq_length=8192 while trained at 512: 27,575 ms -> 14,965 at 512 -> 4,088 at 256 for the same 10 real candidates. Separately it loads fp32 on GPU; the dtype gate covers the embedder only. Both unfixed and recorded rather than silently corrected.",
    "6_cpu_and_gpu_embeddings_differ": "CPU loads float32, GPU loads the checkpoint bfloat16, so vectors differ and one borderline query flips: recall@10 0.925 vs 0.950, MRR effectively tied (0.782 vs 0.785). The numeric difference is sub-1%; the ranking effect is one query of 40."
  },
