  "bugs_found": [
    "rerank was impossible to configure from a file: the section was key-checked against {provider, options, top_n} while option extraction assumed flat siblings, so every shape of a non-`none` provider was rejected. Fixed; tests added.",
    "rerank therefore could not be exercised, which is why the previously recorded eval/results/hybrid_qwen3-0.6b_rerank_bge-v2-m3.json (recall@10 0.875, p50 20,489 ms) had no reproducible config path.",
    "trace resolves bare symbol names only: 'Class.method' and 'path/file.py:symbol' both return 'No trace found'. Pre-existing.",
    "evaluate --skills reported top1_accuracy 0.0 with no skills indexed, indistinguishable from a broken router. Now an error.",
    "ruff check . reached stray root scripts and --fix rewrote them. Now pinned to project code."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "One corpus, one machine, no repeated runs. p50 varies run to run (rerank ranged 12.7-20.5 s across three runs).",
    "Rerank quality is model-dependent; a code-tuned cross-encoder may behave differently. This says THIS model hurts THIS corpus.",
    "hybrid_cpu was measured with no competing load, via eval/measure_index.py against the already-built index, so its latency is directly comparable.",
    "'~55 min on CPU' is one run and includes parsing and SQLite writes, not only embedding."
